
                                                DELETEBLOCK COMMAND


Deletes an infoblock.

Below is the syntax :
                  deleteBlock 	-igErr {"true"|"false"}  -blkid blockId  -igRelink {"true"|"false"}

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -igerr      |    If value is "true" then even if the block is not present in the hex file, it is ignored. If it
               |    is "false", HexmodX aborts with an error saying the block is not present in the file. Mandatory
               |    switch.
   -blkid      |    Block Id of the infoblock to be deleted. Mandatory switch.
   -igrelink   |    If value is "true" then after the deletion of the infoblock, all other blocks will NOT be
               |    relinked. If it is "false", HexmodX will relink all the remaining blocks in the same order as it
               |    was linked earlier. Mandtory switch.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	read -in medc18.hex
	deleteblock -blkID 0x61 -igErr false -igRelink false
	write -out output.hex -lyt 0x20
	
